// m_point_step: a 4-arm `match` over `&mut Point` that was the last
// `structs_enums.vpr` failure (304/305), now verifying (305/305).
// Auto-minimized by a dependency-closure extraction from the real
// `m_point_step` (37 declarations down from 209, comments/dead labels
// stripped by hand; ~18x smaller, ~2s vs the full file's ~7s).
//
// The shape: `&mut Point` is a reference-cell predicate (`p_Ref_mutable`)
// holding the pointee's address generically (`p_Param`); every match arm
// converts it to a concrete `p_Point` and back. CFG linearization scales
// each arm's convert/reconvert by its branch flag, so the `p_Param` chunk's
// permission at the exit `ensures` exhale is a *sum* of four `ite` terms,
// one `ite(discr==k, 1/1, 0/1)` per arm. `lt-ite` cannot descend the `+`
// at the top of that sum, so the sufficiency comparison stayed opaque and
// the discriminant split candidates were invisible to the case-split tier
// (a "candidate unreachable from below") -- the exhale failed regardless of
// budget.
//
// Fixed by `merge_ite_sum` (context.rs), reached from `prove_perm_ineq` on a
// failed sufficiency goal: merge same-condition summands
// (`ite(c,a,x)+ite(c,b,y) => ite(c, a+b, x+y)`), collapsing the nested
// indicator partition to `ite(∨ discr==k, 1, 0)` in O(N) — no case split, any
// arm count. See `perm_cycle_explanation.md` / `findings_2026-07-15.md` §6-7
// for the original diagnosis, and `enum_match_ref_mut_perm_cycle.vpr` for the
// clean no-struct repro (which scales by hand out to 10 arms).

